IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mrca-member`
IMPORT `mrca-guide`

-- Guide to Determining Impairment and Compensation 2026, Chapter 23 -- worked cases, from the member's seat (REQ-0108).
-- Expected values are the Guide's own worked examples and figures read from Tables 23.1 and 23.2 in the deposited text
-- (F2026L00595), worked by hand; never copied from the encoding's output.

-- The Guide's example: Petty Officer Andrews, non-warlike service, 15 impairment points, lifestyle 1: factor .155; at a maximum
-- of $245.82 a week, $38.1021 (the Guide prints $38.10).
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `non-warlike service, including peacekeeping` 15 1 EQUALS JUST 0.155
#ASSERT `What weekly amount does the Guide give me` `non-warlike service, including peacekeeping` 15 1 245.82 EQUALS JUST 38.1021
-- Captain Brown's figures read from the tables: 44 points, lifestyle 4: .478 (Table 23.1) and .268 (Table 23.2).
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `warlike service` 44 4 EQUALS JUST 0.478
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `peacetime service` 44 4 EQUALS JUST 0.268
-- Hazardous service takes the peacetime table (s 67(2)(a)(ii)).
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `hazardous service` 44 4 EQUALS JUST 0.268
-- Warrant Officer Smith's: 42 points, lifestyle 4: .461 and .258.
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `warlike service` 42 4 EQUALS JUST 0.461
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `peacetime service` 42 4 EQUALS JUST 0.258
-- 80 points or more: the maximum, whatever the lifestyle rating or service.
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `peacetime service` 80 0 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `warlike service` 95 3 EQUALS JUST 1
-- The tables have no rows for 1 to 4 points (below every s 69 threshold): not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `warlike service` 3 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A lifestyle rating outside 0 to 7: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my compensation factor` `warlike service` 20 8 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Mixed service (Chapter 23, combined ratings). Captain Brown: A 20 warlike, B 30 peacetime, C 44, L 4:
-- (20 x .478 + 30 x .268) / 50 = 0.352; at $421.72 (1 July 2024), $148.44544 (the Guide prints $148.45).
#ASSERT `the mixed compensation factor` 20 30 44 4 EQUALS JUST 0.352
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for mixed service` 20 30 44 4 421.72 EQUALS JUST 148.44544
-- The conditions the other way round: (30 x .478 + 20 x .268) / 50 = 0.394; $166.15768 (printed $166.16).
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for mixed service` 30 20 44 4 421.72 EQUALS JUST 166.15768
-- Warrant Officer Smith: A 30, B 20, C 42, L 4: (30 x .461 + 20 x .258) / 50 = 0.3798 by the formula (the Guide prints
-- 0.380 and $160.25; finding 13); $160.169256.
#ASSERT `the mixed compensation factor` 30 20 42 4 EQUALS JUST 0.3798
#ASSERT `What weekly amount for mixed service` 30 20 42 4 421.72 EQUALS JUST 160.169256

-- The lump sum choice on the Guide's amount (s 78(1)). Andrews: .155 of the maximum, between 10% and 20%: all or half.
#ASSERT `What share may I convert, on the Guide's amount` `non-warlike service, including peacekeeping` 15 1 245.82 EQUALS JUST (LIST 50, 100)
-- 80 points: the whole maximum, more than 20%: 25, 50, 75 or 100 per cent.
#ASSERT `What share may I convert, on the Guide's amount` `peacetime service` 80 2 245.82 EQUALS JUST (LIST 25, 50, 75, 100)
-- 3 points: no table row, so no amount and no choice.
#ASSERT `What share may I convert, on the Guide's amount` `peacetime service` 3 0 245.82 EQUALS NOTHING
